# Pins the local runner image act uses, so `act` runs are reproducible.
# catthehacker/ubuntu is a community-maintained image that approximates the real
# (much larger) GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest runner more closely than plain `ubuntu`.
#
#   act -j test            run the CI job locally before pushing
#
# act needs a container runtime. ms-01-2 has neither Docker nor Podman, so there the
# fallback is to run the same two gates by hand against the PINNED ruff:
#
#   ruff check . && ruff format --check .
#   pytest tests -q
#
# The pin is what matters: CI once installed ruff 0.17.3 against a local 0.15.14 and
# failed 61 checks that passed locally.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
